{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 11 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Task7 {\n    static class FastScanner {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n\n        FastScanner(File f) {\n            try {\n                br = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(f));\n            } catch (FileNotFoundException e) {\n                e.printStackTrace();\n            }\n        }\n\n        FastScanner(InputStream f) {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(f));\n        }\n\n        String nextLine() {\n            try {\n                return br.readLine();\n            } catch (IOException e) {\n                return null;\n            }\n        }\n\n        String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreTokens()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    e.printStackTrace();\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n\n        double nextDouble() {\n            return Double.parseDouble(next());\n        }\n\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        FastScanner in = new FastScanner(System.in);\n        int n = in.nextInt();\n        int B = in.nextInt();\n\n        int[] values = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            values[i] = in.nextInt();\n        }\n\n        int evens = 0, odds = 0;\n        PriorityQueue<Integer> pq = new PriorityQueue<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {\n            if (values[i] % 2 == 0) evens++;\n            else odds++;\n            if (evens == odds) {\n                pq.offer(Math.abs(values[i] - values[i + 1]));\n            }\n        }\n\n        int result = 0;\n        while (!pq.isEmpty() && B >= pq.peek()) {\n            B -= pq.poll();\n            result++;\n        }\n        System.out.println(result);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <fstream>\n#include <queue>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <string>\n#include <sstream>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nclass FastScanner {\nprivate:\n    BufferedReader* br;\n    vector<string> tokens;\n    int tokenIndex;\n\npublic:\n    FastScanner(const string& filename) {\n        br = new BufferedReader(filename);\n    }\n\n    FastScanner() {\n        br = new BufferedReader();\n    }\n\n    string nextLine() {\n        return br->readLine();\n    }\n\n    string next() {\n        while (tokenIndex >= tokens.size()) {\n            string line = br->readLine();\n            if (line.empty()) return \"\";\n            istringstream iss(line);\n            tokens.clear();\n            tokenIndex = 0;\n            string token;\n            while (iss >> token) {\n                tokens.push_back(token);\n            }\n        }\n        return tokens[tokenIndex++];\n    }\n\n    int nextInt() {\n        return stoi(next());\n    }\n\n    long nextLong() {\n        return stol(next());\n    }\n\n    double nextDouble() {\n        return stod(next());\n    }\n};\n\nclass BufferedReader {\nprivate:\n    istream* in;\n\npublic:\n    BufferedReader(const string& filename) {\n        in = new ifstream(filename);\n    }\n\n    BufferedReader() {\n        in = &cin;\n    }\n\n    string readLine() {\n        string line;\n        if (getline(*in, line)) {\n            return line;\n        }\n        return \"\";\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    FastScanner in;\n    int n = in.nextInt();\n    int B = in.nextInt();\n\n    vector<int> values(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        values[i] = in.nextInt();\n    }\n\n    int evens = 0, odds = 0;\n    priority_queue<int, vector<int>, greater<int>> pq;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {\n        if (values[i] % 2 == 0) evens++;\n        else odds++;\n        if (evens == odds) {\n            pq.push(abs(values[i] - values[i + 1]));\n        }\n    }\n\n    int result = 0;\n    while (!pq.empty() && B >= pq.top()) {\n        B -= pq.top();\n        pq.pop();\n        result++;\n    }\n    cout << result << endl;\n\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001776060671545565, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.000773250067140907, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -2.074220174108632e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -2.145764938177308e-06, -0.8594915866851807, -2.264974000354414e-06, -5.602679812000133e-05, -6.079655122448457e-06, -0.5956945419311523, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.0967194612021558e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.01173933781683445, -7.152555099310121e-07, -2.0265558760002023e-06, 0.0, -0.844393253326416, -0.0010333680547773838, -0.0017047885339707136, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.0561630427837